A||||3||Taijiguy||Ignition system RPM capability||||5||
Z||000000||Taijiguy||08-14-2000||08:05 AM||||Does anyone here have an educated idea of the capability if the stock electronic ignition? My 2.8 goes flat at a little over 5,000 rpm. (remember I have the ECM completely stripped- Edelborck intake, Holley 390 4bbl, etc. I installed a vacuum advance distributor from an 84 Blazer (still has the ignition module, but doesn't use an ECM) So I'm wondering if the 5000RPM disruption is the result of the ignition, or if my valves are starting to float at that point. (Stock springs, high lift cam)<BR>Any ideas?<P>Thanks,<P>-Taiji||||reg||5
Z||000001||elfiero||08-14-2000||09:30 AM||||I've had some experiance with this problem.<BR>you are correct in suspecting the HEI,the<BR>module usally takes a crap around 5000RPM.<BR>there is a company that makes an improved<BR>module fairly cheap.I think the name is<BR>Davis unified ignition,and I think they<BR>are located in ohio.Next, you might want to<BR>make sure you are not running out of fuel-<BR>I dont know what you did for the fuel pump,<BR>but I sure you changed somthing when you put<BR>on the carb.Last but not least,it's my opinion that your valve train should be good<BR>to 6000-provided you dont stay there long!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||08-14-2000||11:29 AM||||Thanks for the confirmation. I don't think fuel is the problem, since the carb has bowls on it, not like the injection. Basically, what I did was keep the stock pump, and connect the supply and reurn lines to a TEE, and then tap off the tee to supply the carb. I put a hose clamp around the supply line and tightened it until the pressure was so high it overcame the closed needle valve, and overflowed the fuel bowls, and then backed off a bit. SO I'm sure fuel supply is plenty sufficient. I may need to work on the valve trin some more though. I think I'd like to be able to run up to 6500 or so, I know the motor will do it. (after all, I *DID* build it...)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000003||PJ||08-14-2000||09:10 PM||||I don't think its the module unless its aftermarket. Although I run with the rev limiter usually set at 6,400 I have run it up to 7,000 accidently on occasion without any problems (rev limiter doesn't work on downshifts). Runs fine for an hour and a half between 4 and 6.5 grand. No module problems unless the motor overheats. Stock distributor, pick-up coil and OEM module. Accel ignition coil mounted off the motor, 8mm wires, rapidfires and a chip are the only mods. Might be the valve train as you mentioned. The stock springs are pretty weak to use with a high lift cam.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black||||reg||1
